    fact_meteorite: 'Space rocks really hit Mars. The InSight lander felt one hit in December 2021. It made a crater about 150 meters wide.',
    fact_leak: 'Even the space station has had air leaks. Small cracks in one tunnel have leaked air since 2019, and NASA watches them closely.',
    fact_marsTime: 'A Mars day is longer than an Earth day. Rover teams on Mars time started work about 40 minutes later every day.',
    fact_astronautBlood: 'Scientists studied the blood of six astronauts before and after a flight. Genes for repairing DNA and handling stress changed.',
    fact_mars520: 'Six people once lived for 520 days in a pretend trip to Mars, so scientists could study how being cut off changes body and mood.',

    learn_health_t: 'Your health bar', learn_health: 'Green is your health. You can heal it with rest, food and the doctor. Purple is radiation. It never heals, so your bar gets shorter. Try it!',
    learn_meteor_t: 'Space rocks!', learn_meteor: 'Mars has very thin air, and real space rocks hit it. NASA felt them with a sensor on the ground. Press the button.',
    learn_leak_t: 'Air leak!', learn_leak: 'Mars air cannot keep you alive, so the base must stay sealed. If a wall leaks, patch it fast.',
    learn_help_t: 'Help your team!', learn_help: 'When someone is badly hurt they cannot move. A teammate must reach them in time. Nobody survives on Mars alone.',
